From 54e7f9443e3f7d674970826ece6d4b08138f0535 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kartikya Motwani <kartikya@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 04:27:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate stock-chart and live-price endpoints to Angel One
 (PRICE_FEED=angel)

Extends the PRICE_FEED switch beyond just the live bot's tick loop to
the Research/Discover pages, which were still hitting yfinance and
getting rate-limited (YFRateLimitError seen in production logs today).

New: app/services/angel_feed.py::get_angel_ohlc(symbol, period) - daily
OHLC via Angel's getCandleData, same output shape ({time, open, high,
low, close}) as historical_data.fetch_ohlc_for_chart so it's a drop-in.
Maps period strings ("5d".."5y","max") to a fromdate/todate range;
"max" is capped at 10 years as a practical stand-in since Angel has no
true "max" like yfinance. Reuses the same auth-error-detection and
one-retry-with-fresh-login logic already built for get_angel_ltp.

Wired into routes.py: /discover/stock-chart/{symbol},
/prices/{symbol}/live, and /prices/live now check settings.PRICE_FEED
and call the Angel functions when set to "angel", otherwise unchanged
yfinance behavior (default stays "yahoo").

NOT migrated, and documented clearly why: /discover/stock-info/{symbol}
(company fundamentals - sector, market cap, P/E, 52-week high/low).
Angel One's SmartAPI is a trading + market-data API with no
fundamentals/research endpoint at all - there's nothing on Angel's
side to move this to. That one endpoint keeps its yfinance
rate-limit exposure regardless of PRICE_FEED.

Verified: get_angel_ohlc's candle-parsing tested against a realistic
mocked getCandleData response (Angel's documented format: list of
[iso_timestamp, open, high, low, close, volume] rows) - correctly
produces the expected {time, open, high, low, close} shape. All 17
existing tests still pass. NOT live-tested against Angel's real
getCandleData endpoint - verify a couple of chart periods actually
render on the Research page before relying on this fully.
